      "message": "#### Usage in NetworkPolicyManagerService\n* NPMS has build[SnoozeWarning|SnoozeRapid]Intent() methods will put a template to an Intent. The receiver is also NPMS, it registers [mSnoozeReceiver](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d1297) for ACTION_SNOOZE_WARNING and ACTION_SNOOZE_RAPID. Also, the templates used by these two Intents are from `mNetworkPolicy` which are [read from disk](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java;l\u003d2628;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1) and created by NetworkTemplate.Builder().\n* The other two methods, build[NetworkOverLimit|ViewDataUsage]Intent() are for notification activity. NetworkOverLimit intent looks like it\u0027s for [NetworkOverLimitActivity](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/net/NetworkOverLimitActivity.java;l\u003d50?q\u003dEXTRA_NETWORK_TEMPLATE\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.\u0026start\u003d1). And ViewDataUsage is for DataUsageSummaryActivity which extends SettingsActivity. I don\u0027t know how SettingsActivity uses the template but the templates to be put into NetworkOverLimit and ViewDataUsage Intents are from `mNetworkPolicy` which are read from disk and created by NetworkTemplate.Builder().\n* Considering that netpolicy.xml stores template on disk and it might contain subscriberIdMatchRule and subscriberId (subscriberId would be removed in follow-up patch), it needs to check if this change breaks the xml file.\n * In current design, when [write subscriberIdMatchRule](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java;l\u003d2797;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1) to xml file, it\u0027s decided by if the `subscriberIds` in the template is empty or not. And SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_ALL and SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_EXACT have no dependency on module since they are in static library. The usage of subscriberIdMatchRule here is that there\u0027s a value of subscriberIdMatchRule in the xml file and we use it when read netpolicy.xml to decide if the `subscriberIds` should be set. This is probably fine but we may need to remove the usage of subscriberIdMatchRule from NPMS.\n * [subscriberId](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java;l\u003d2792;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1) is obtained by `template.getSubscriberIds().iterator().next()`, which means that the subscriberId is not obtained by any API provided by NetworkTemplate. So it looks probably fine if remove subscriberId from NetworkTemplate and it\u0027s also need to remove the usage of subscriberId from NPMS.\n \n#### Usage in Settings app\n\n* DataUsagePreferenceController.init()\n→ fetchMobileTemplate() → DataUsageLib.getMobileTemplate() and [DataUsageLib](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/datausage/lib/DataUsageLib.java;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5;l\u003d95?q\u003dDataUsageLib\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.) generate the NetworkTemplate by NetworkTemplate.Builder(). This is for [DataUsagePrefernceController.getNetworkTemplate()](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/network/telephony/DataUsagePreferenceController.java;l\u003d107;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5?q\u003dEXTRA_NETWORK_TEMPLATE\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.\u0026start\u003d11) to return a template.\n* It looks like that the DataUsagePreferenceController.handlePreferenceTreeClick() is triggered by [DashboardFragment.onPreferenceTreeClick()](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/dashboard/DashboardFragment.java;l\u003d237?q\u003dhandlePreferenceTreeClick\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject:packages%2Fapps%2FSettings%2F\u0026start\u003d191) and it calls getNetworkTemplate to get a template to put into the intent.\n* Template used in DataUsagePreference it\u0027s set by setTemplate(), there are 2 classes use DataUsagePreference.\n  * [WifiSettings](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/wifi/WifiSettings.java;l\u003d275?q\u003dsetTemplate\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject:packages%2Fapps%2FSettings%2F\u0026start\u003d1) and [NetworkProviderSettings](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/network/NetworkProviderSettings.java;l\u003d326?q\u003dsetTemplate\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject:packages%2Fapps%2FSettings%2F\u0026start\u003d1), and both use NetworkTemplate.Builder() to create a template\n* Template used in DataUsageSummay, there are 3 methods use template\n * [addMobileSection](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/datausage/DataUsageSummary.java;l\u003d171;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5?q\u003dTemplatePreferenceCategory\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.): get template by DataUsageLib.getMobileTemplate\n * [addWifiSection](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/datausage/DataUsageSummary.java;l\u003d184;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5?q\u003dTemplatePreferenceCategory\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.): Use NetworkTemplate.Builder\n * [addEthernetSection](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/src/com/android/settings/datausage/DataUsageSummary.java;l\u003d190;drc\u003dcb3bd7c37d630acb613e10f730c532128a02a3d5?q\u003dTemplatePreferenceCategory\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.): Use NetworkTemplate.Builder\n \n#### Usage in NetworkPolicy\n* There\u0027s no usage related to [subscriberIdMatchRule](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/NetworkPolicy.java;l\u003d330?q\u003dNetworkPolicy.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.) and the subscriberId is obtained by subscriberIds list. It looks fine for NetworkPolicy.",
